  "label": "User projected onto the textual material",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material because the text uses second-person deictic pronouns ('you', 'your') which directly address the viewer, making the viewer feel personally implicated in the scenario described. The text 'when your fifth wife...' creates an implicit 'you' that the user is expected to identify with, projecting the user's perspective onto the offensive narrative.",
